🚽 Test case: #196 -- a struct/union-tagged pointer's initializer is
🚽 checked against the DECLARED TAG, not just "is this a struct pointer"
🚽 (PR #248 review, round 2, finding 1). VAR_STRUCT is a category, not a
🚽 type: `gang Point` and `gang Rect` are both VAR_STRUCT, pointer_level
🚽 1, so the round-1 fix's category-only check (declared_type == init_type)
🚽 passed this silently, then followed the pointer using Point's layout
🚽 on an actually Rect-shaped blob.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};
gang Rect {
    rizz w;
    rizz h;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Rect r;
    r.w = 11;
    r.h = 22;
    gang Point *pp = &r;
    yapping("%d %d", pp.x, pp.y);
}
